// Coefficients for the audio x8 interpolator (rtl/audio/audio_interp_x8.v), read with
// $readmemh. One 18-bit two's complement hex value per line (5 hex digits), 144 values in
// direct-form tap order h[0]..h[143]; the RTL re-derives the 8 polyphase phases from this same
// order (phase p, tap k = h[8k+p], i.e. line number 8k+p+1). See docs/A1_AUDIO.md for the
// filter design (144-tap FIR, Parks-McClellan/remez, passband 0-18 kHz, stopband from 28 kHz,
// Q17 fixed point) and tools/gen_audio_interp_coeffs.py, which generated this file and must be
// re-run if the filter design changes (do not hand-edit).
